Object subclass: #NvRasterKernels
	instanceVariableNames: ''
	classVariableNames: 'Cubin'
	package: 'System-Devices'!

NvRasterKernels comment: 'I am generated by tools/nv-kernels.py from gpu/nv/raster.cu and gpu/nv/raster_abi.h (SHA-256 of the two 9845f1c1337d5c36) with nvcc -cubin -arch=sm_121 -O3 -fmad=false (Build cuda_13.0.r13.0/compiler.36424714_0); do not edit me, regenerate me (docs/nv-kernels.md). I hold the raster kernels: PlatformRaster''s work (SoftwareRaster: the Renderer''s uber-shader on a draw''s vertices, fills, blits, copies) as CUDA kernels for the NVIDIA GB10 (sm_121), bit-exact with the C reference without floating-point contraction, and their ABI, for a launcher that loads the cubin itself (no CUDA libraries).

	NvRasterKernels cubin                         "the ELF image: 379520 bytes, SHA-256 4518a326a7920a6f1bcf6898d884142475e5e6c4b1fac368d9f409b8a2f22fa7"
	NvRasterKernels kernel: ''raster_tiles''        "its entry, parameter struct, registers, shared memory, constant banks"
	NvRasterKernels params: #RasterDrawParams with: {#pixels -> a. #width -> 1920. ...}   "the parameter bytes"

A draw is raster_prims then raster_tiles with the same RasterDrawParams; fills, copies and blits are one launch each. Parameters go into constant bank 0 at the kernel''s paramOffset; a kernel with constantBank2 needs those bytes bound as constant bank 2. Grids and blocks: docs/nv-kernels.md.'!

!NvRasterKernels class methodsFor: 'cubin'!
cubin
	"The kernels' ELF image (decoded once)."
	| out |
	Cubin isNil ifTrue: [
		out := WriteStream on: (ByteArray new: self cubinSize).
		self cubinBase64 do: [:each | out nextPutAll: (Base64 decode: each)].
		Cubin := out contents].
	^Cubin
!
